\newlabel{fig:noc-physical-design}{{5}{4}{Physical NoC organization. The Mesh, added corner attachments, and combined placement describe one network in the same Logic tier. Each CS contains four 3:1 MUXes with selection and enable inputs driven by the NI responsible for that CS. One drawn corner attachment represents separate transmit and receive data bundles}{figure.caption.9}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Design of an NPU node. The NI contains packet classification, configuration reception and storage, separate Mesh and CS receive FIFOs, and the local buffer-write interface. Its stored controls select one auxiliary transmit branch and one receive branch, and drive its owned CS. Separate reverse-control wires return credits from the CS receive FIFO through the configured RX, CS, and TX selections to the transmitting router.}}{4}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:noc-node}{{6}{4}{Design of an NPU node. The NI contains packet classification, configuration reception and storage, separate Mesh and CS receive FIFOs, and the local buffer-write interface. Its stored controls select one auxiliary transmit branch and one receive branch, and drive its owned CS. Separate reverse-control wires return credits from the CS receive FIFO through the configured RX, CS, and TX selections to the transmitting router}{figure.caption.10}{}}
